format session-log-v1
stamp 20260815.001200
editor Zed
model Fable 5
voice Kyri
host Ubuntu cloud pier — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES102 — Lotus's smoothed silence trim, smooth the runs before stripping so the strip declicks the pause and keeps the gap
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first; after ALES101 sent, take the next agent-doable Lotus lap, self-approve, prove GREEN, send as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think ALES101 built the smoothing hysteresis; this rung is where it pays off, which makes it the Lindy crux of the whole silence family. ALES96 strips every silent run from the RAW segmentation, and the raw segmentation flickers: a single loud tick buried in a pause reads voiced, so ALES96 keeps the click; a single quiet frame between two words reads silent, so ALES96 cuts the gap and the words run together. Both are exactly the artefacts an editor complains about. Run ALES101 before the strip and both vanish — the tick, shorter than min_run, is relabeled to the silence around it and stripped; the short gap, shorter than min_run, is relabeled to the speech around it and kept. One knob turns a literal silence remover into a speech-aware one: remove the dead air, spare the breath, drop the click.
think Shape is ALES96 with one stage inserted — segment, smooth (ALES101), cut the smoothed silent runs. ALES101's coverage law is what makes this safe: the smoothed runs tile the same span exactly (same starts, same total), so every smoothed silent run is a valid original-clip span, cut back to front exactly as ALES96 cuts. No new error — SmoothTrimError is ALES96's TrimError with ALES101's SmoothError (only the unreachable SegmentsFull) reused by name.
think Proved four laws. The min-zero law: smooth_trim(min=0) equals ALES96's trim_silence byte for byte over a grid (8 frame lengths x 4 floors x 3 splits) — min=0 is identity smoothing, so ALES102 is a strict generalization sharing its boundary. The concat law: the result equals the hand-built concatenation of the non-silent SMOOTHED runs over 8 min_run values, so it can never drift. The declick law: silent(8)·voiced tick(4)·silent(8) — the raw trim keeps the 4 tick samples, smooth_trim(min=8) empties, strictly shorter, the click gone. The keep-gap law: voiced(8)·silent gap(4)·voiced(8) — the raw trim cuts the gap to 16, smooth_trim(min=8) keeps all 20, strictly longer, the breath preserved. I did NOT claim monotonicity in min_run and stated why: a larger min_run removes more clicks yet keeps more gaps, so length can rise or fall — the declick and keep-gap laws are the two honest sides of that.
obs First witness run GREEN on the first pass — the min-zero grid (96), the concat grid (8), the declick and keep-gap laws each proving strictly-shorter and strictly-longer against the raw trim on the same signal, an all-silent clip emptying at three mins, a no-silent clip unchanged at three mins, and four named refusals. TAME style bans clean, width-check exit 0.
obs No custody gate reached — software only, local; no funds, keys, network, device, or real speaker. It edits only by removing whole smoothed-silent frames through ALES2's cut, fabricating no sample and reordering nothing.
loom witness=ales_smooth_trim_witness green=1 laws=4 min_zero_grid=96 concat_grid=8 module_bytes=15k
file lotus/smooth_trim.rye ALES102 — smooth_trim() segments, smooths through ALES101, then cuts the smoothed silent runs back to front; the min-zero twin of ALES96.
file tools/ales_smooth_trim_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs the selftest, asserts the GREEN line.
file active-designing/20260815-001200_fill-ales102-lotus-smoothed-silence-trim.md the self-approved design read naming the min-zero, concat, declick, and keep-gap laws and the honest non-monotonicity.
file lotus/README.md front door — the ALES102 rung appended to the roster and the stamp synced.
recommend keep-going — the next Lotus crux stays in the family: a smoothed collapse (ALES100 fed the smoothed runs so a capped pause never keeps a click), a symmetric two-sided smoother that also rescues a too-short opening run this causal hold cannot, or a min-gap merge that smooths only silent runs; each its own self-approved round, no custody gate reached.
